    {
      "id": "5botc8n",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.1 Making of the Constitution"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Making of the Constitution outlines the historical trajectory and assembly debates shaping India's democracy.",
        "The Preamble serves as the introductory statement highlighting the core values, aims, and philosophy of the Constitution.",
        "Fundamental Rights are listed under Part III (Articles 12–35) and guarantee basic civil liberties to citizens.",
        "Directive Principles of State Policy in Part IV (Articles 36–51) guide the state in formulating social and welfare policies.",
        "Fundamental Duties are incorporated under Article 51-A, setting civic obligations for citizens.",
        "Key Constitutional Amendments modify and adapt the Constitution to modern socio-political needs."
      ],
      "id": "avykfl9"
    },
