      "content": "7.6 Important Constitutional Articles"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Crucial distinction tested in exams: Fundamental Rights (Part III) are justiciable, whereas Directive Principles (Part IV) are non-justiciable.",
        "Article 51-A (Fundamental Duties) was added by the 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1976 based on the Swaran Singh Committee recommendations.",
        "Frequently tested items include landmark Constitutional Amendments and constitutional remedies under Article 32."
      ],
      "id": "f0cm8gv"
